# ============================================================================
#  Docker build context filter   (build context = ./app)
#
#  Entries here are dropped BEFORE the daemon ever receives the context, so an
#  excluded file cannot end up in an image layer. That matters beyond image
#  size: layers are immutable and are published with the image, so a secret
#  copied in by accident is a secret published — deleting it in a later layer
#  does not remove it from the earlier one.
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Build artifacts — the only entries that matter for context SIZE.
#
#  A host `target/` is hundreds of MB, is linked against the host's libc, and
#  is unusable inside the builder. Shipping it also defeats the layer cache:
#  its contents change on every host `cargo build`, so the `COPY . ./` layer
#  is invalidated on every image rebuild even when no source changed.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.profraw
*.profdata

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Version control and CI metadata — no runtime value, and `.git/` carries the
#  full history of every file ever committed, including ones since removed.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.gitlab-ci.yml

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Docker's own files. The daemon already holds the Dockerfile out of band; a
#  compose file inside the image only leaks the deployment topology.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yaml
docker-compose*.yml

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Credentials and key material.
#
#  NOTE: `config.toml` is deliberately NOT excluded — задание 2 requires the
#  config file to be packed into the image. It therefore must never hold a
#  password: credentials reach the process through the environment (задание 2)
#  or through Vault (задание 6).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519
.netrc
.pgpass
.vault-token
vault-data/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Editor and OS cruft
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  SAST / DAST output and scratch state (задания 8–10). The reports are graded
#  deliverables in the repository; they have no reason to sit in a runtime
#  image, and a CodeQL database is larger than the image itself.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
codeql-db/
*-codeql-db/
.codeql/
.scannerwork/
.sonar/
.semgrep/
zap-session/
*.sarif
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/coverage/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Logs, scratch, editor backups
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
*.pid
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
tmp/
scratch/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Documentation — never read at runtime.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.md
